---
// TODO(Jacob): This is a plain-language template, not legal advice.
// Have it reviewed (ideally by a lawyer) before relying on it, and update
// LAST_UPDATED when you change it.
// [LEGAL: REVIEW]: Confirm jurisdiction-specific recording disclosures, consent, and retention terms before relying on this template.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LegalContact from "../components/LegalContact.astro";
import { BUSINESS_NAME, EMAIL, LEGAL_ENTITY, PHONE } from "../config";
import { filled } from "../lib/site";

const LAST_UPDATED = "October 25, 2026";
const entity = filled(LEGAL_ENTITY) ? LEGAL_ENTITY.trim() : BUSINESS_NAME;
const named = entity === BUSINESS_NAME ? entity : `${entity} ("${BUSINESS_NAME}")`;
const hasContact = filled(EMAIL) || filled(PHONE);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | OJ Solutions"
  description="How OJ Solutions collects, uses, and shares your information, including text messages."
>
  <article>
    <header class="on-navy">
      <div class="container-page pt-12 pb-12 sm:pt-16 sm:pb-16">
        <h1 class="display-1">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-soft mt-4 text-lg">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="container-page pt-6 pb-16 sm:pt-10 sm:pb-24">
      <div class="prose-page max-w-2xl">
        <p>
          This policy explains what information {named} ("we," "us") collects through this website and when you contact
          us, how we use it, and the choices you have. We keep it in plain language on purpose.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>What you give us.</strong> When you book a call, fill out a form, text us, or email us, we collect what
            you share, such as your name, email, phone number, business name, and what you tell us about your business.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Basic technical information.</strong> Like most websites, our hosting provider may log basic details
            such as your IP address, browser type, and the pages you visit, to keep the site running and secure.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Consultation requests.</strong> Our 15-minute request form collects your preferred date
            and time, name and email, and any optional phone, business name, service, and message. This is stored in the
            secure OJ Workspace database operated through our infrastructure provider. Requests aren't confirmed
            appointments until we contact you.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>AI receptionist demo calls.</strong> When you call our AI front desk, it identifies itself as an AI
            assistant. Calls may be recorded and transcribed so we can handle inquiries and review how the system works.
            Please do not provide sensitive personal information in a demonstration call.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How we use it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To respond to you and schedule calls.</li>
          <li>To provide the services you ask for.</li>
          <li>To send messages about your inquiry or appointment, including text messages only when you've specifically opted in.</li>
          <li>To keep our website working and secure.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Text messages (SMS)</h2>
        <p>
          If you choose the optional, unchecked SMS-consent box on our consultation request form, we may text
          you about that consultation. Providing a phone number without checking the box is not SMS consent.
          Any marketing text campaign requires separate permission.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>
              We do not share mobile numbers or SMS opt-in consent with third parties or affiliates for marketing or
              promotional purposes.
            </strong>{" "}
            Text messaging opt-in data and consent are never shared with any third parties.
          </li>
          <li>Message frequency varies.</li>
          <li>Message and data rates may apply.</li>
          <li>Reply <strong>STOP</strong> to opt out at any time. Reply <strong>HELP</strong> for help.</li>
          <li>Agreeing to receive texts is not a condition of buying anything from us or requesting a consultation.</li>
          <li>When you opt into texts through our consultation form, we store that choice and its timestamp alongside the inquiry.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>
          We don't sell your information. We share it only with service providers that help us run our business, such as
          our scheduling, CRM, email, and website hosting providers, and only so they can do that work for us. We may
          also share information if the law requires it. All of the above excludes text messaging opt-in data and
          consent, which we never share with third parties.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We keep your information for as long as we need it to work with you and to meet legal or accounting
          requirements. After that, we delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us what information we have about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it.{
            hasContact && " Just reach out using the contact details below."
          }{" "}You can stop text messages at any time by replying STOP.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>This website is meant for businesses. It's not directed to children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their information.</p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If we change this policy, we'll post the new version here and update the date at the top.</p>

        <LegalContact topic="this policy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
